# AWS SBG MEC portal - live Firebase config. Copy to .env for local dev. Never commit .env.
# cp .env.example .env
#
# 1) WEB APP KEYS - where to copy each value:
#    Firebase Console > Project Settings > General > Your apps > Web app > SDK setup and configuration.
#    Click the web app (create one if none), choose Config, copy each field below.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=placeholder-api-key-replace-me
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=placeholder.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=placeholder-project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=placeholder.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=placeholder-sender-id
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=placeholder-app-id
# Required for live: API_KEY + AUTH_DOMAIN + PROJECT_ID + APP_ID.
# STORAGE_BUCKET and MESSAGING_SENDER_ID are optional for this Firestore-only build.
# Any missing key or value still containing placeholder/example/changeme shows
# the live-required error with zero rows.
VITE_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=5000

# 2) AUTH SETUP (manual, no env needed):
#    a. Firebase Console > Build > Authentication > Sign-in method > enable Email/Password.
#    b. Authentication > Users > Add user > create the moderator email + password.
#    c. Copy the new user's UID, then grant admin ONE of these ways:
#       Option A (custom claim): firebase auth:set-custom-user-claims <uid> '{"is_admin": true}'
#       Option B (allowlist doc): create Firestore doc admins/<uid> with any field,
#         e.g. { "email": "host@example.com" }.
#    d. Sign in at /admin. If you used a claim, sign out and back in to refresh the token.

# 3) FIRESTORE SETUP:
#    a. Firebase Console > Build > Firestore Database > Create database (production mode, region closest to hall).
#    b. Deploy rules + composite indexes from repo root:
#       firebase deploy --only firestore
#       (uses firestore.rules + firestore.indexes.json via firebase.json)
#    c. The wall query where(status in [approved, featured]) + orderBy(created_at) needs the
#       composite index. Deploy before doors open or the wall fails with a missing-index error.
#
# Notes kept from live runbook:
# - Long-polling is forced in code for college WiFi. Polling every 5s + Refresh now stays on.
# - Client rate limit stays: 3 posts per minute per browser.
# - No answers UI in this version. Questions only.
